## 🔒 Middleware Patterns (NEW)

### User-Siswa Validation Middleware
```javascript
// File: backend/middleware/userSiswaValidation.js

const validateUserSiswa = async (req, res, next) => {
  try {
    const { userId, siswaId } = req.params;
    
    if (userId && siswaId) {
      // Validate relationship exists
      const [result] = await db.execute(
        'SELECT 1 FROM siswa WHERE id_siswa = ? AND user_id = ?',
        [siswaId, userId]
      );
      
      if (result.length === 0) {
        return res.status(400).json({
          success: false,
          error: 'User-Siswa relationship invalid'
        });
      }
    }
    
    next();
  } catch (error) {
    console.error('Validation error:', error);
    res.status(500).json({ error: 'Validation failed' });
  }
};

// Usage
app.get('/api/siswa/:siswaId/user/:userId', 
  authenticateToken,
  validateUserSiswa,
  async (req, res) => {
    // Handler
  }
);
```

## 📋 Best Practices (UPDATED)

### 1. Always Use Transactions for Multi-Table Operations
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT
let connection;
try {
  connection = await db.getConnection();
  await connection.beginTransaction();
  
  await connection.execute('INSERT INTO users...');
  await connection.execute('INSERT INTO siswa...');
  
  await connection.commit();
} catch (error) {
  if (connection) await connection.rollback();
  throw error;
} finally {
  if (connection) connection.release();
}
```

### 2. Check user_id for NULL Before Using
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT
if (siswa.user_id) {
  // Has user account - can login
  const [userData] = await db.execute('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = ?', [siswa.user_id]);
} else {
  // No user account - data only
  console.log('Student has no login account');
}
```

### 3. Normalize Role in JWT Token
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Always lowercase in token, uppercase in DB
const tokenPayload = {
  id: user.id,
  role: user.role === 'perwakilan' ? 'siswa' : user.role.toLowerCase(),
  username: user.username
};
```

### 4. Smart Delete Strategy
```javascript
// ✅ CORRECT: Check history before delete
const [attendance] = await db.execute(
  'SELECT COUNT(*) as count FROM absensi_siswa WHERE siswa_id = ?',
  [siswaId]
);

if (attendance[0].count > 0) {
  // Has history - deactivate
  await db.execute('UPDATE users SET status = "tidak_aktif"...');
} else {
  // No history - hard delete
  await db.execute('DELETE FROM users...');
}
```

## 🚨 Error Handling (UPDATED)

### Standard Error Response Format
```javascript
// Success response
res.json({
  success: true,
  data: {...},
  message: 'Operation completed successfully'
});

// Error response
res.status(errorCode).json({
  success: false,
  error: 'Error type',
  message: 'User-friendly error message',
  details: {...} // Optional
});
```

### Common Error Codes
- `400` - Bad Request (validation errors)
- `401` - Unauthorized (invalid/missing token)
- `403` - Forbidden (insufficient permissions)
- `404` - Not Found (resource not found)
- `409` - Conflict (duplicate data)
- `500` - Internal Server Error

